        "title": "Formal Semantics: Montague Grammar",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "For TCS background: Montague grammar IS typed lambda calculus applied to natural language. The semantic metalanguage is Church's simple type theory. Compositionality is the Frege principle formalized as a homomorphism. If you understand denotational semantics of programming languages, you understand the architecture of Montague semantics."
